# Root .env.example — the variables the off-serving CLIs and probes read
# (ingestion, eval, snapshots, migrations). Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill
# in. The SERVING process does NOT read this file: on the VPS its whole
# configuration is `/etc/kajianq/api.env` (root:root 0600), documented by
# provision/vps/api.env.example — see docs/VPS-OPERATIONS.md §1.3.
#
# Post-ADR-0044 the serving host is the netcup VPS. There is no Cloudflare
# Worker, no Alchemy stack file, and no Neon: the database is self-hosted and
# reached over TCP. The vendor-free name below reflects that (ADR-0044
# decision 5) — a hosting move must not look like a storage-engine change.

# Postgres over TCP — the self-hosted VPS database. Used by the migration CLI
# (`db:*` scripts), the RagStore contract suite, the eval harness, and the
# snapshot tooling. Locally, a tunnel to the box works:
#   ssh -L 15433:127.0.0.1:5432 kajianq-deploy@<host>   # then use :15433
# In CI it arrives as the STAGING_DATABASE_URL secret (already the tunnel port).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://kajianq:CHANGE_ME@127.0.0.1:5432/kajianq

# R2 S3-compatible access for the ingestion CLI and the snapshot/db tooling
# (buckets kajianq-raw and kajianq-raw-staging). These keys are for
# off-serving scripts only — the serving path never touches object storage
# (raw-corpus archival is a CLI concern, ADR-0044). Read by
# packages/infra/scripts/{r2-verify,snapshot-store}.mjs and
# packages/kajianq-domain/scripts/archive-store.mjs.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET_STAGING=kajianq-raw-staging
R2_BUCKET_PROD=kajianq-raw

# Optional error tracking (free tier). Both DSNs unset = Sentry fully disabled.
# SENTRY_DSN is the API's own DSN: on the box it lives in /etc/kajianq/api.env
# (provision/vps/api.env.example); leave it unset locally to keep Sentry off.
# SENTRY_DSN=
# Web build-time errors-only reporting (Session Replay is opt-in, see apps/web/src/lib/sentry.ts):
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# Provider API keys for local/CLI use — the serving host holds its own copies in
# /etc/kajianq/api.env. Names are the `apiKeyEnv` entries in
# packages/infra/src/providers/models.json (ADR-0009/ADR-0022); config decides
# which roles they may serve. Never commit a real value.
#   DEEPSEEK_API_KEY    generator/router AND reviewer head (personal-data allowed)
#   GEMINI_PAID_API_KEY embedder head (paid terms; the free-tier Gemini row is
#                       refused for personal-data calls by design)
#   GEMINI_API_KEY      free-tier Gemini — non-personal calls (ingestion, tagging)
#   DASHSCOPE_API_KEY   catalogued generator challenger (optional)
# DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_PAID_API_KEY=

# Ingestion CLI source/report dirs (issues #6, #7). Setting a SOURCE_DIR
# makes the CLI reuse cached source files for offline re-runs; a REPORT_DIR
# writes the run's IngestionReport JSON alongside the eval_runs ledger row.
# QURAN_SOURCE_DIR=
# HADITH_SOURCE_DIR=
# HADITH_REPORT_DIR=
# HADITH_EDITIONS_BASE_URL=

# Rate-limit bypass signer key (ADR-0041): base64 PKCS8 Ed25519 private key.
# The matching public key is committed (apps/api/src/lib/rate-bypass.ts) and
# verifies `X-Rate-Bypass` JWTs that exempt harness requests (schemathesis,
# ZAP, load tests) from the /v1 per-IP budget — metering only, never auth.
# Mint with `bun run rate:bypass`. Mirror the same value as the GitHub
# Actions secret RATE_BYPASS_PRIVATE_KEY for the Staging workflow.
# RATE_BYPASS_PRIVATE_KEY=
